        "original_id": "1cbbe4ea-d54c-5f62-a370-227bca0d1373",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Michael Kanin, Ring Lardner Jr.\n- Films: Woman of the Year, When I Grow Up, Sredni Vashtar\n- Awards: Academy Awards, BAFTA Award for Best Short Film\n- Topics: Hollywood blacklist, Red Scare\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Kanin was born on February 1, 1910, and he later became an American director, producer, playwright, and screenwriter.\n- Ring Lardner Jr. was born on August 19, 1915, and he later became an American journalist and screenwriter.\n- In 1942, Michael Kanin shared an Academy Award with Ring Lardner Jr. for writing the Katharine Hepburn-Spencer Tracy film comedy Woman of the Year.\n- Ring Lardner Jr. was blacklisted by Hollywood movie studios during the Red Scare of the late 1940s and 1950s.\n- When I Grow Up is a 1951 American drama film written and directed by Michael Kanin.\n- Sredni Vashtar won the BAFTA Award for Best Short Film and was nominated for an Academy Award.\n- Michael Kanin died on March 12, 1993.\n- Ring Lardner Jr. died on October 31, 2000.",
